-- title:
--   Archimedean Jacobian of ξ↦σ(ξ)-λ'ξ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Put $E = L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$ is the infinite adele ring of $K$, equipped with a measurable space structure that is the Borel structure of its topology, and let $\lambda$ be an additive Haar measure on $E$. Let $\lambda'$ be a unit of $E$ and assume that $1 - N_{E/\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}}(\lambda')$ is a unit of $\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$, where $N$ denotes the algebra norm of $E$ over $\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$. Let $G : E \to [0,\infty]$ be measurable. Then $$\Big(\prod_{v \mid \infty} \big\|\big(1 - N(\lambda')\big)_v\big\|^{m_v}\Big) \int_E G\big(\sigma(\xi) - \lambda'\xi\big)\, d\lambda(\xi) = \int_E G\, d\lambda,$$ the product being over the infinite places $v$ of $K$, with $m_v$ the multiplicity of $v$ ($1$ for real, $2$ for complex) and $(\cdot)_v$ the component of an infinite adele at $v$; here $\sigma(\xi)$ means the image of $\xi$ under the ring homomorphism [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaTensor`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L199), namely $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$ on $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$, and the scalar factor is read as an element of $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   This is the archimedean Jacobian computation for the twisted substitution $\xi \mapsto \sigma(\xi) - \lambda'\xi$ on $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$: the substitution scales additive Haar measure by $\prod_{v\mid\infty}\|1-N\lambda'\|_v^{m_v}$. It feeds the estimate of twisted orbital integrals over the torus used in the base-change comparison underlying the Langlands–Tunnell input.
